<div class="dt-post-body"><div class="available-content"><div dir="auto" class="body markup"><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2w3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM" class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2w3w!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2w3w!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2w3w!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2w3w!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"/><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2w3w!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png" width="940" height="788" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/edb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:788,&quot;width&quot;:940,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:1175855,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2w3w!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2w3w!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2w3w!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2w3w!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fedb0e4d3-e838-478d-9e7b-7e20284354f6_940x788.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high" class="sizing-normal"/></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p><span>AuDHD (autism + ADHD) can feel like living with two operating systems at once: one craves pattern, predictability, and sensory truth; the other craves novelty, urgency, and dopamine. When you add </span><strong>alexithymia</strong><span> (trouble identifying/putting words to feelings) and </span><strong>anhedonia</strong><span> (reduced interest/pleasure), it can feel like your inner world is running on </span><em>silent mode</em><span>—or like emotions are happening in the background, but the app won’t open.</span></p><p>This isn’t a personal failure. It’s brain wiring, body signals, and overload physics.</p><p><span>Let’s break down what these are, why they show up so often in neurodivergent lives, how they affect kids </span><em>and</em><span> adults, and what actually helps—plus journal prompts that feel like a flashlight, not a courtroom.</span></p><div><hr/></div><h2 class="header-anchor-post">What is alexithymia?<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§what-is-alexithymia" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/what-is-alexithymia" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p><strong>Alexithymia</strong><span> is a trait (not a diagnosis) involving:</span></p><ul><li><p>difficulty identifying feelings</p></li><li><p>difficulty describing feelings</p></li><li><p>a tendency toward “externally oriented thinking” (focusing on facts/tasks over inner states)</p></li></ul><p>In plain language: your body may be broadcasting emotion… but your brain is struggling to translate the signal into words.</p><h3 class="header-anchor-post">The neuroscience-y “why”<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§the-neuroscience-y-why" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/the-neuroscience-y-why" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p><span>A big piece here is </span><strong>interoception</strong><span>—your brain’s ability to notice and interpret internal body signals (heart rate, tight chest, nausea, heat, hunger, fatigue). Research suggests alexithymia is strongly linked with interoceptive differences, and in autism research, alexithymia (not autism traits alone) can explain certain interoceptive difficulties.</span></p><p>So if your internal signals are “blurry,” emotions often become:</p><ul><li><p><strong>mystery symptoms</strong><span> (headache, stomach drop, jaw clench, sudden irritability)</span></p></li><li><p><strong>surprise explosions</strong><span> (because the warning signs didn’t register clearly)</span></p></li><li><p><strong>shutdowns</strong><span> (because the system gets overwhelmed and pulls the plug)</span></p></li></ul><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sZIf!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM" class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sZIf!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sZIf!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sZIf!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sZIf!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"/><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sZIf!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png" width="1456" height="971" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:971,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:3059134,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sZIf!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sZIf!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sZIf!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sZIf!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F806e55b4-0519-4d5d-b04a-1eeb08204c3e_1536x1024.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy" class="sizing-normal"/></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p></p><h3 class="header-anchor-post">How common is it in autism and ADHD?<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§how-common-is-it-in-autism-and-adhd" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/how-common-is-it-in-autism-and-adhd" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p><span>A major review found alexithymia prevalence in autistic groups ranging roughly </span><strong>33%–63%</strong><span>, with a weighted average around </span><strong>~50%</strong><span> in the studies reviewed. </span><br/><span>And in one adult ADHD sample, alexithymia showed up at a notably higher rate in the ADHD group than controls.</span></p><p>For AuDHD folks, it’s not rare—it’s a frequent roommate.</p><div><hr/></div><h2 class="header-anchor-post">What is anhedonia?<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§what-is-anhedonia" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/what-is-anhedonia" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p><strong>Anhedonia</strong><span> is </span><strong>markedly reduced interest or pleasure</strong><span> in activities that used to feel good. It can show up as:</span></p><ul><li><p><span>“I </span><em>know</em><span> I like this… but I can’t feel it.”</span></p></li><li><p>“Nothing sounds appealing.”</p></li><li><p>“Even fun feels like effort.”</p></li></ul><p>Clinically, anhedonia is a core symptom in depression and other conditions, but it can also appear with burnout, chronic stress, trauma responses, and neurodivergent overload cycles.</p><h3 class="header-anchor-post">Two flavors that matter<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§two-flavors-that-matter" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/two-flavors-that-matter" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p>Researchers often talk about:</p><ul><li><p><strong>anticipatory pleasure</strong><span> (“wanting” / motivation / looking forward to it)</span></p></li><li><p><strong>consummatory pleasure</strong><span> (“liking” / enjoyment in the moment)</span></p></li></ul><p>You can have either one disrupted—like wanting without liking, or liking without wanting (hello, “I enjoy it once I start, but starting is impossible”).</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p4Q1!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM" class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p4Q1!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p4Q1!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p4Q1!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p4Q1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"/><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p4Q1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png" width="1456" height="971" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:971,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:3329385,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p4Q1!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p4Q1!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p4Q1!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p4Q1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F714ac7ec-ec3d-42a8-8c38-7bf12a5cd628_1536x1024.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy" class="sizing-normal"/></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><h3 class="header-anchor-post">The brain circuitry piece<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§the-brain-circuitry-piece" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/the-brain-circuitry-piece" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p><span>Anhedonia is tightly tied to </span><strong>reward processing</strong><span>—especially circuits involving the </span><strong>ventral striatum/nucleus accumbens</strong><span> and dopamine signaling.</span></p><p>And here’s where AuDHD comes in:</p><ul><li><p>ADHD research often finds atypical reward processing and dopaminergic signaling differences involving striatal circuits, which can show up as motivation problems and “now vs later” friction.</p></li><li><p>Autism research includes evidence for differences in social reward “wanting” and ventral striatal responses in some contexts—meaning social rewards may not reliably light up the brain’s reward engine the same way, especially under stress/uncertainty.</p></li></ul><div><hr/></div><h2 class="header-anchor-post">Why alexithymia + anhedonia can travel together in AuDHD<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§why-alexithymia-anhedonia-can-travel-together-in-audhd" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/why-alexithymia-anhedonia-can-travel-together-in-audhd" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p>Picture this like a two-step problem:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Alexithymia</strong><span> makes it harder to </span><em>identify what you feel and need</em><span>.</span></p></li><li><p><strong>Anhedonia</strong><span> makes it harder to </span><em>access the “this feels good” signal that fuels motivation and connection.</em></p></li></ol><p>So the brain loses both:</p><ul><li><p><span>the </span><strong>map</strong><span> (what’s going on inside me?)</span></p></li><li><p><span>and the </span><strong>reward beacon</strong><span> (what would help and feel good?)</span></p></li></ul><p>And when you can’t name what’s wrong, you can’t target support. When you can’t feel reward, your brain stops trying. That’s not laziness—that’s conservation mode.</p><p>Add AuDHD factors:</p><ul><li><p>sensory overload</p></li><li><p>masking</p></li><li><p>executive dysfunction</p></li><li><p>social uncertainty fatigue</p></li><li><p>demand avoidance / threat responses to pressure</p></li></ul><p>…and your nervous system starts treating daily life like a low-grade emergency.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!d3zm!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM" class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!d3zm!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!d3zm!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!d3zm!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!d3zm!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"/><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!d3zm!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png" width="1456" height="971" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/a5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:971,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:3499224,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!d3zm!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!d3zm!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!d3zm!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!d3zm!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa5f024ee-91b4-430c-8ed2-ba0cc4bc86b3_1536x1024.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy" class="sizing-normal"/></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><div><hr/></div><h2 class="header-anchor-post">How this can look in adults<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§how-this-can-look-in-adults" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/how-this-can-look-in-adults" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><h3 class="header-anchor-post">Alexithymia in adults can sound like:<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§alexithymia-in-adults-can-sound-like" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/alexithymia-in-adults-can-sound-like" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><ul><li><p><span>“I don’t know how I feel. I just know I’m </span><em>off</em><span>.”</span></p></li><li><p>“I’m fine.” (translation: I have no data)</p></li><li><p>“I’m not emotional.” (translation: I don’t have labels, not that I lack feelings)</p></li><li><p><span>conflict that escalates fast because the </span><em>first recognized emotion is the big one</em></p></li></ul><p><span>It can also impact relationships because feelings don’t get communicated early—so partners/friends only see the </span><strong>shutdown</strong><span> or </span><strong>snap</strong><span>, not the slow build.</span></p><h3 class="header-anchor-post">Anhedonia in adults can look like:<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§anhedonia-in-adults-can-look-like" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/anhedonia-in-adults-can-look-like" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><ul><li><p>doomscrolling because nothing else lands</p></li><li><p>losing interest in hobbies, music, intimacy, food, social plans</p></li><li><p>“I can’t start fun, only obligations” (and even those are brutal)</p></li><li><p>emotional flatness that scares you because you remember being someone who felt things</p></li></ul><p>Important reality check: anhedonia can be a depression signal. If it’s persistent, worsening, or paired with hopelessness, sleep/appetite changes, or thoughts of self-harm—loop in a clinician. Not because you’re broken, but because you deserve backup.</p><div><hr/></div><h2 class="header-anchor-post">How this can look in kids<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§how-this-can-look-in-kids" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/how-this-can-look-in-kids" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p><span>Kids often don’t have the vocabulary even </span><em>without</em><span> alexithymia. With AuDHD + alexithymia/anhedonia, it can show up as behavior, not words.</span></p><h3 class="header-anchor-post">Alexithymia-ish patterns in kids:<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§alexithymia-ish-patterns-in-kids" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/alexithymia-ish-patterns-in-kids" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><ul><li><p>lots of “I don’t know” when asked about feelings</p></li><li><p>big reactions that seem “out of nowhere”</p></li><li><p>body complaints (tummy, headache) instead of emotion labels</p></li><li><p><span>difficulty with empathy </span><em>language</em><span> even if they care deeply</span></p></li><li><p>trouble explaining what happened after a meltdown (“I forgot,” “nothing,” “he did it”)</p></li></ul><h3 class="header-anchor-post">Anhedonia-ish patterns in kids:<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§anhedonia-ish-patterns-in-kids" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/anhedonia-ish-patterns-in-kids" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><ul><li><p>less interest in play they used to love</p></li><li><p>“meh” response to rewards that used to work</p></li><li><p>social withdrawal or “parallel-only” preference increasing</p></li><li><p>irritability replacing joy (very common—especially in kids)</p></li></ul><p><span>And because AuDHD kids can live in chronic overwhelm, what looks like “not interested” may be </span><strong>protected capacity</strong><span>: their nervous system is rationing energy.</span></p><div><hr/></div><h2 class="header-anchor-post">The sneaky thing: shutdown can masquerade as anhedonia<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§the-sneaky-thing-shutdown-can-masquerade-as-anhedonia" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/the-sneaky-thing-shutdown-can-masquerade-as-anhedonia" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p>Sometimes the issue isn’t “I can’t feel pleasure” so much as:</p><ul><li><p><span>I’m </span><strong>overloaded</strong></p></li><li><p><span>I’m </span><strong>dissociated</strong></p></li><li><p><span>I’m </span><strong>shutdown</strong></p></li><li><p><span>I’m </span><strong>depleted</strong></p></li><li><p><span>I’m </span><strong>unsafe</strong></p></li></ul><p>When safety drops, pleasure drops. Joy is not a moral achievement; it’s a nervous system permission slip.</p><div><hr/></div><h2 class="header-anchor-post">Supports that actually help<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§supports-that-actually-help" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/supports-that-actually-help" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p>Podcast Reccomendation: </p><div data-component-name="DigestPostEmbed" class="digestPostEmbed-flwiST"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-reset"><a href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/p/authentically-adhd-adhd-alexithymia" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><h2 class="pencraft pc-reset color-pub-primary-text-tsxVWu line-height-36-XWjwZY font-display-JL8OCo size-30-GcF1QW weight-bold-Bp7iNJ reset-PDs18X">Authentically ADHD – ADHD, Alexithymia, and Anhedonia: Understanding Emotions and Motivation</h2></a><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-4 pc-alignItems-center pc-reset"><div class="pencraft pc-reset color-pub-secondary-text-X0WYlZ line-height-20-_MEacI font-meta-Wq5ZQP size-11-gJkq5q weight-medium-Hv9lSX transform-uppercase-LYgH6s reset-PDs18X meta-SjvJkP"><a href="https://substack.com/profile/109463432-carmen_authenticallyadhd" class="inheritColor-WetTGJ">carmen_authenticallyadhd</a></div><div class="pencraft pc-reset color-pub-secondary-text-X0WYlZ reset-PDs18X">·</div><div class="pencraft pc-reset color-pub-secondary-text-X0WYlZ line-height-20-_MEacI font-meta-Wq5ZQP size-11-gJkq5q weight-medium-Hv9lSX transform-uppercase-LYgH6s reset-PDs18X meta-SjvJkP">July 5, 2025</div></div><div class="pencraft pc-paddingTop-24 pc-reset"><a href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/p/authentically-adhd-adhd-alexithymia" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!uFO0!,w_424,h_212,c_fill,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6bb58e4b-57ba-4244-b354-9cdb3463f0db_3000x3000.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!uFO0!,w_848,h_424,c_fill,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6bb58e4b-57ba-4244-b354-9cdb3463f0db_3000x3000.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!uFO0!,w_1272,h_636,c_fill,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6bb58e4b-57ba-4244-b354-9cdb3463f0db_3000x3000.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!uFO0!,w_1300,h_650,c_fill,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6bb58e4b-57ba-4244-b354-9cdb3463f0db_3000x3000.png 1300w" sizes="100vw"/><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!uFO0!,w_1300,h_650,c_fill,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6bb58e4b-57ba-4244-b354-9cdb3463f0db_3000x3000.png" sizes="100vw" alt="Authentically ADHD – ADHD, Alexithymia, and Anhedonia: Understanding Emotions and Motivation" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!uFO0!,w_424,h_212,c_fill,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6bb58e4b-57ba-4244-b354-9cdb3463f0db_3000x3000.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!uFO0!,w_848,h_424,c_fill,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6bb58e4b-57ba-4244-b354-9cdb3463f0db_3000x3000.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!uFO0!,w_1272,h_636,c_fill,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6bb58e4b-57ba-4244-b354-9cdb3463f0db_3000x3000.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!uFO0!,w_1300,h_650,c_fill,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6bb58e4b-57ba-4244-b354-9cdb3463f0db_3000x3000.png 1300w" width="1300" height="650" class="img-OACg1c fullWidth-Ta6aEE pencraft pc-reset"/></picture></a></div><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-paddingTop-16 pc-reset flex-grow-hUPOlM"><p class="caption-QiPycG">Authentically ADHD – ADHD, Alexithymia, and Anhedonia: Understanding Emotions and Motivation</p></div><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-16 pc-paddingTop-0 pc-paddingBottom-0 pc-alignItems-center pc-reset"><a href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/p/authentically-adhd-adhd-alexithymia" class="pencraft pc-reset align-center-OkiSzE line-height-20-_MEacI font-text-a4IB2X size-13-yQMlsX weight-medium-Hv9lSX reset-PDs18X"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-alignItems-center pc-reset link-HREYZo"><span class="pencraft pc-reset color-accent-ycT0qD line-height-20-_MEacI font-text-a4IB2X size-14-XNg_Ct weight-semibold-LL37we reset-PDs18X">Listen now</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></div></a></div></div></div><h3 class="header-anchor-post">1) Build an “emotion translation” bridge (body → word → need)<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§1-build-an-emotion-translation-bridge-body-word-need" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/1-build-an-emotion-translation-bridge-body-word-need" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p>Because if feelings are subtitles, we can generate them manually.</p><p><strong>Tools:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Emotion wheel (start with 6 basic emotions, then get fancy)</p></li><li><p>Body map: “Where do I feel it?”</p></li><li><p>Sentence stems:</p><ul><li><p>“I might be feeling ___ because ___.”</p></li><li><p>“My body is doing ___, which might mean ___.”</p></li><li><p>“If this feeling had a job, it would be trying to ___.”</p></li></ul></li></ul><p><strong>Micro-skill goal:</strong><span> not perfect accuracy—</span><em>better signal.</em><br/><span>Interoception + alexithymia links make this a high-impact target.</span></p><div><hr/></div><h3 class="header-anchor-post">2) Use interoception training like it’s a superpower, not homework<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§2-use-interoception-training-like-its-a-superpower-not-homework" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/2-use-interoception-training-like-its-a-superpower-not-homework" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p>Try 30–60 seconds, 1–3 times a day:</p><ul><li><p>heart: fast/steady?</p></li><li><p>breath: shallow/deep?</p></li><li><p>jaw/shoulders: tight/soft?</p></li><li><p>stomach: open/knotted?</p></li><li><p>temperature: warm/cold?</p></li><li><p>energy: drained/ok/buzzy?</p></li></ul><p><span>Then label </span><strong>one</strong><span> word: </span><em>tense, heavy, buzzy, blank, tender, sharp.</em></p><p>You’re building the “signal clarity” pipeline.</p><div><hr/></div><h3 class="header-anchor-post">3) Separate pleasure from performance<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§3-separate-pleasure-from-performance" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/3-separate-pleasure-from-performance" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p>AuDHD brains often turn hobbies into jobs. Then anhedonia strolls in like, “Congrats, now nothing is fun.”</p><p><strong>Rule:</strong><span> pick activities with </span><strong>no output requirement</strong><span>.</span></p><ul><li><p>sensory pleasures (warm shower, weighted blanket, sour candy, crunchy snacks, music in the dark)</p></li><li><p>“process hobbies” (doodling, organizing beads, knitting, miniature kits)</p></li><li><p>nature + movement snacks</p></li></ul><div><hr/></div><h3 class="header-anchor-post">4) Treat reward like a timid cat: gentle, consistent, no sudden grabbing<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§4-treat-reward-like-a-timid-cat-gentle-consistent-no-sudden-grabbing" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/4-treat-reward-like-a-timid-cat-gentle-consistent-no-sudden-grabbing" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p><span>When reward systems are glitchy, the answer isn’t “try harder.”</span><br/><span>It’s </span><strong>smaller, sooner, more certain</strong><span>.</span></p><p>ADHD reward research repeatedly highlights “now vs later” friction and the importance of immediacy/feedback loops.</p><p><strong>Try:</strong></p><ul><li><p>2-minute start + immediate micro-reward</p></li><li><p>“after I start, I can stop” rule (reduces threat)</p></li><li><p>visual progress (stickers, checkmarks, done lists)</p></li><li><p>body doubling for activation (social dopamine without heavy social demand)</p></li></ul><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r2hG!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM" class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r2hG!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r2hG!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r2hG!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r2hG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"/><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r2hG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png" width="1456" height="971" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:971,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:3499879,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r2hG!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r2hG!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r2hG!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r2hG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4576d9e9-091a-467c-aaf2-cfdb1ffea511_1536x1024.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy" class="sizing-normal"/></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><div><hr/></div><h3 class="header-anchor-post">5) Build “safe joy” on purpose (especially for kids)<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§5-build-safe-joy-on-purpose-especially-for-kids" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/5-build-safe-joy-on-purpose-especially-for-kids" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p>For kids, think: predictable, sensory-friendly, low-demand.</p><p><strong>Examples:</strong></p><ul><li><p>“Joy menu” board with pictures (3 choices only)</p></li><li><p>routine “connection rituals” (same song + cuddle, same book + snack)</p></li><li><p>parallel play invitations (“I’ll build next to you”)</p></li><li><p>interest-based social (dinosaurs > small talk)</p></li></ul><p>Autism reward research suggests that motivation and “wanting” can be context-sensitive—so make the context safer and more predictable, and you often get more access to engagement.</p><div><hr/></div><h3 class="header-anchor-post">6) Name needs before they become symptoms<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§6-name-needs-before-they-become-symptoms" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/6-name-needs-before-they-become-symptoms" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p>Alexithymia can make needs hard to detect—so we externalize.</p><p><strong>Daily needs checklist (adult + kid friendly):</strong></p><ul><li><p>Food?</p></li><li><p>Water?</p></li><li><p>Movement?</p></li><li><p>Quiet?</p></li><li><p>Pressure/comfort?</p></li><li><p>Temperature change?</p></li><li><p>Social break?</p></li><li><p>Transition buffer?</p></li><li><p>Task clarity?</p></li></ul><p><span>If you can’t identify feelings, identify </span><strong>conditions</strong><span>.</span></p><div><hr/></div><h3 class="header-anchor-post">7) Get clinical backup when the joy-loss is persistent<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§7-get-clinical-backup-when-the-joy-loss-is-persistent" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/7-get-clinical-backup-when-the-joy-loss-is-persistent" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p>If anhedonia lasts weeks, worsens, or comes with depression symptoms, it’s worth a professional screen. Anhedonia is a recognized clinical feature in mood disorders, and it’s treatable—but it often needs more than self-help tools.</p><div><hr/></div><h2 class="header-anchor-post">Reflection prompts: flashlight, not courtroom<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§reflection-prompts-flashlight-not-courtroom" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/reflection-prompts-flashlight-not-courtroom" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><h3 class="header-anchor-post">A. Alexithymia-friendly prompts (body-first)<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§a-alexithymia-friendly-prompts-body-first" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/a-alexithymia-friendly-prompts-body-first" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><ol><li><p><strong>My body today is saying:</strong><span> (tight / heavy / buzzy / blank / tender / hot / cold)</span></p></li><li><p><strong>The loudest signal is:</strong><span> (jaw / chest / stomach / head / shoulders)</span></p></li><li><p><span>If this sensation could talk, it would ask for </span><strong>one</strong><span> thing: ___</span></p></li></ol><h3 class="header-anchor-post">B. Anhedonia-friendly prompts (permission + tiny steps)<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§b-anhedonia-friendly-prompts-permission-tiny-steps" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/b-anhedonia-friendly-prompts-permission-tiny-steps" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><ol start="4"><li><p>What’s one thing I used to like that feels far away right now?</p></li><li><p><span>What version of that could be </span><strong>10% smaller</strong><span> and still count?</span></p></li><li><p>What’s a “safe pleasure” I can access even when I’m flat? (texture, warmth, water, music, pressure, light)</p></li></ol><h3 class="header-anchor-post">C. AuDHD reality prompts (reduce shame, increase accuracy)<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§c-audhd-reality-prompts-reduce-shame-increase-accuracy" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/c-audhd-reality-prompts-reduce-shame-increase-accuracy" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><ol start="7"><li><p><span>Am I uninterested—or am I </span><strong>overloaded</strong><span>? What’s my best guess?</span></p></li><li><p>What demand is my nervous system interpreting as threat right now?</p></li><li><p><span>What would make today feel </span><strong>more navigable</strong><span> (not perfect)?</span></p></li></ol><h3 class="header-anchor-post">D. Connection prompts (for adults, partners, parents)<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§d-connection-prompts-for-adults-partners-parents" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/d-connection-prompts-for-adults-partners-parents" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><ol start="10"><li><p>If I could communicate one sentence about my inner world today, it would be:</p></li><li><p>The kindest interpretation of my behavior this week is:</p></li><li><p>One support I can ask for without overexplaining is:</p></li></ol><h3 class="header-anchor-post">E. Kid-friendly versions (simple + concrete)<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§e-kid-friendly-versions-simple-concrete" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/e-kid-friendly-versions-simple-concrete" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><ul><li><p>My body feels: ☐ fast ☐ slow ☐ tight ☐ wiggly ☐ heavy ☐ tired</p></li><li><p>I might need: ☐ snack ☐ quiet ☐ squeeze ☐ help ☐ break ☐ move</p></li><li><p>One thing that helps me feel better is: ___</p></li></ul><div><hr/></div><h2 class="header-anchor-post">A closing note (because you deserve one)<div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class="pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id="§a-closing-note-because-you-deserve-one" class="pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div><button tabindex="0" type="button" aria-label="Link" data-href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/i/186406461/a-closing-note-because-you-deserve-one" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p>If you grew up thinking you were “bad at feelings,” I want you to hear this clearly:</p><p>You are not cold. You are not broken. You are not failing at being human.</p><p><span>You’re running a brain-body system that sometimes sends signals in riddles and sometimes mutes the reward channel to conserve power. The work isn’t to become a different person. The work is to build </span><strong>translation tools</strong><span>, reduce </span><strong>overload</strong><span>, and create </span><strong>safe pathways back to pleasure</strong><span>—one tiny, stubborn step at a time.</span></p><p></p><p data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/p/audhd-alexithymia-and-anhedonia-when/comments&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Leave a comment&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton" class="button-wrapper"><a href="https://carmenauthenticallyadhd.substack.com/p/audhd-alexithymia-and-anhedonia-when/comments" class="button primary"><span>Leave a comment</span></a></p><div class="subscription-widget-wrap"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p>This Substack is reader-supported. To receive new posts and support my work, consider becoming a free or paid subscriber.</p></div><div data-component-name="SubscribeWidget" class="subscribe-widget"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-justifyContent-center pc-reset"><div class="container-IpPqBD"><form action="/api/v1/free?nojs=true" method="post" novalidate class="form form-M5sC90"><input type="hidden" name="first_url" value/><input type="hidden" name="first_referrer" value/><input type="hidden" name="current_url"/><input type="hidden" name="current_referrer"/><input type="hidden" name="first_session_url" value/><input type="hidden" name="first_session_referrer" value/><input type="hidden" name="referral_code"/><input type="hidden" name="source" value="subscribe-widget-preamble"/><input type="hidden" name="referring_pub_id"/><input type="hidden" name="additional_referring_pub_ids"/><input type="hidden" name="source_post_id" value="186406461"/><div class="sideBySideWrap-vGXrwP"><div class="emailInputWrapper-QlA86j"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-minWidth-0 pc-position-relative pc-reset flex-auto-UL7Y7f"><input name="email" placeholder="Type your email..." aria-label="Email" type="email" class="pencraft emailInput-OkIMeB input-y4v6N